# THE SHIP: the players' flying magic ship (GameShip, Entities/Game/airship.pre). BLOCKY: everything is whole 2 m grid
# tiles - 28 x 11 tiles (56 x 22 m; the bow z -28, the stern +28, the beam x -10 .. 12). y = 0 is the DECK TOP (the
# walk surface); the keel's bottom is y = -7 (GameShip::KeelDepth). The outline is a half-width in tiles per 2 m row
# (the same table as GameShip::makeBody, which builds the collider from it) around a CENTRE COLUMN (the tile x 0 .. 2:
# the middle line is x = 1, the origin stays on a tile corner): a bow that narrows a tile every two rows, the widest
# beam a little forward of the middle, a broad flat stern. Under the deck tier (2 m) two tiers step in by a
# tile each side and start further back at the bow (the stem rakes), then the keel. The WALL is not here: it is the
# ShipRail structures on the edge tiles (Entities/Game/shipRail.pre). Objects, one render piece each:
#   ShipHull - the tiers and the keel   ShipDeck / ShipDeckB - the deck planks, one per tile column, two tones
#   ShipTrim - the wale along the sides, the bowsprit and the rudder
# GENERATED: axis-aligned boxes, all pieces share one UV and the six normals: 1 +X  2 -X  3 +Y  4 -Y  5 +Z  6 -Z
